{"ts":"2026-07-26T18:31:20.767Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"a31af454c29fc92c25cebfd4","op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-07-26T18:31:20.767Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Dependency-drift sweep 2026-07-26 (live npm query, whole manifest).\n\nRuntime and toolchain drift, current -> latest:\n\n| package | current | latest | gap |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| @toon-format/toon | 2.3.1 | 4.1.0 | **two majors** |\n| npm-package-arg | 13.0.2 | 14.0.0 | one major |\n| typescript | 6.0.3 | 7.0.2 | one major |\n| @sentry/node | 10.67.0 | 10.68.0 | patch |\n| typebox | 1.3.7 | 1.3.8 | patch |\n\npnpm audit reports 0 vulnerabilities at every severity (info/low/moderate/\nhigh/critical all zero), and GitHub Dependabot shows 0 open alerts, so none of\nthis is a security exposure. It is a maintenance-currency finding.\n\nWhy the TOON row is the one that matters here rather than the TypeScript row:\nTOON is the default output encoding for the entire agent-facing surface\n(output_default: \"toon\"), so this dependency sits on every read path an agent\ntouches. Published majors are 0, 1, 2 and 4 across 20 versions — the project is\npinned on 2.x while the registry has moved to 4.x, and there is no 3.x, so the\nupgrade is a single two-major step rather than an incremental walk.\n\nThis also intersects an open correctness defect on the same encoder: GH-747\n(pm-hybj) reports that the TOON encoder emits a quoted notes[] scalar its own\ndecoder rejects, making valid tracked items unreadable — the same failure family\nas pm-iqgj (closed), where the strict decoder mis-parsed bracketed tokens and 16\nitem files had to be recovered. Evaluating whether 4.x already fixes the\nencoder/decoder asymmetry is therefore part of this item's scope and may reduce\nit, not just a compatibility exercise.\n\nNo re-file: this evidence is recorded here because pm-5cgm2z already owns the\nTOON 4 evaluation and item-format migration."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-26T18:31:20.767Z"}],"before_hash":"f53f76e3b08e4b8a1dace29d4e2485b0a23894977c9bc3f80de0d74c6174bf90","after_hash":"17c32db0f8fdf92df5153ddcd83a75497266772b81cb1f3f17b06bcace9e9e2f"}
